From b3ee7eb7966e1f10c53df9bba845f11efbfa5b33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 02:18:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 047/102] feat(server): gateway limits - body limit setting,
 receive deadline, per-client cap, classify text checks

max_request_body_mb (default 100) replaces cpp-httplib's compile-time payload
default. request_receive_timeout (default 0, off) bounds the time from accept
to the route handler, enforced by a watchdog that shuts down a duplicate of the
socket; while it is set each connection carries one request.
max_connections_per_client (default 0, off) refuses further connections from
one address with 503; loopback is exempt. All three rebuild the HTTP listeners
when changed. The onnxruntime and tflite classify backends now refuse text over
1 MiB before forwarding, sharing the check executorch had.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
